## TL;DR — what changed since v2 (2026-05-25)

**Production trusted setup.** All fixtures now use the **Hermez
Perpetual Powers of Tau** ceremony (BN254, K=20 slice of
`powersOfTau28_hez_final.ptau`) — the same 80+-contributor public
ceremony snarkjs, iden3 and Polygon zkEVM use.

The `[s]·G2` point embedded in
`tvm-sdk/tvm_vm/src/executor/zk_halo2_utils.rs::KZG_S_G2_BYTES` is
sourced from the same ceremony, so prover (`bridge-snark-utils`)
and verifier (the AN-side `ZKHALO2VERIFYWITHVK` handler) agree on the
KZG commitment scheme byte-for-byte. `KZG_G0_BYTES` and `KZG_G2_BYTES`
are curve generators (BN254 constants) and didn't change.

To rebuild the SRS locally (≈25 min wall-clock — download + convert +
`same_ratio` validation):

```bash
bash scripts/bootstrap_hermez_srs.sh
```

The script is idempotent (skips already-cached `.ptau` / matching SRS)
and verifies the canonical halo2 SRS via SHA-256
`80394564e2598883dbb5d7d61630287f34e29cdd806d7ef74f68acc6bffeb608`.

Then re-keygen + reprove if you want to regenerate the fixtures:

```bash
rm -f crates/bridge-snark-utils/params/{fallback_pk,fallback_vk,fallback_config_params}.{bin,json}
cd crates/bridge-snark-utils
EXPORT_HALO2_FIXTURE_DIR=fixtures/circuit_1b_fallback \
  cargo test --release --test halo2_tvm_bundle_round_trip -- --nocapture
```

Wall-clock: ~3.5 min keygen + ~14 min prove. The new VK
(`fallback_vk.bin`, 6 154 B) is structurally identical to the old one
(same circuit, same `BaseCircuitParams`) but its commitments are
evaluated against the ceremony's `[s]`, so old `fallback_proof.bin`
WILL NOT verify against new `KZG_S_G2_BYTES` — the whole bundle
(`vk_blob` + `public_inputs` + `proof`) regenerates atomically.

## TL;DR — what changed since v1 (2026-05-22)

`ZKHALO2VERIFYWITHVK` now takes **three stack cells**, not one
self-describing bundle:

```text
   top      proof_cell           raw SHPLONK proof bytes (no header)
   ↑        public_inputs_cell   raw N × 32 LE Fr (no header)
   bottom   vk_cell              VkBlob (magic "VKBLOB\x00\x00" + version
                                  + transcript + config_json + vk_bytes)
```

```text
   PUSHREF vk_cell
   PUSHREF public_inputs_cell
   PUSHREF proof_cell
   ZKHALO2VERIFYWITHVK
```

### Why three cells

| Operand               | Lifetime                                                            |
|-----------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `vk_cell`             | Deploy-time. Stored once in the contract's `c4` / persistent storage. Magic-tagged + versioned so a drifted producer/consumer is rejected loudly. |
| `public_inputs_cell`  | Per-call. Contract builds it O(1) from the call arguments (no header to skip). |
| `proof_cell`          | Per-call. Comes verbatim from off-chain prover output. |

### `vk_cell` payload (`VkBlob`)

```text
   off  size  field
   ───  ────  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     0     8  magic           = b"VKBLOB\x00\x00"
     8     1  version         = 0x01
     9     1  transcript_kind = 0x00 (Blake2b; 0x01 reserved for Keccak)
    10     6  reserved        = 0 × 6
    16     4  config_len   (u32 LE)
    20  cl    config_json  (UTF-8 serde_json of `BaseCircuitParams`)
   ...     4  vk_len       (u32 LE)
   ...  vl    vk_bytes     (`VerifyingKey::write(SerdeFormat::RawBytes)`)
```

`SerdeFormat::RawBytes` runs the on-curve check on every G1 element of
the VK — **mandatory** because the VK is supplied by an untrusted
contract. The producer side at
`crates/bridge-snark-utils/src/halo2_tvm_bundle.rs::VkBlob::from_native`
mirrors this byte layout exactly.

### `public_inputs_cell` payload

No header at all. Just `N × 32` flat little-endian `Fr::to_repr()`
values concatenated. Length must be a multiple of 32; values
`≥ Fr modulus` are rejected as `FatalError` (not a silent
verify-false — caller bug, fail loudly).

### `proof_cell` payload

No header at all. Raw SHPLONK proof bytes from
`Blake2bWrite::<_, _, Challenge255<_>>::finalize()`. Hand them
verbatim to a TVM cell.

## Fixture: Circuit 1B fallback BLS attestation verifier (K=20)

The `fixtures/` directory carries the **real** verification key for
the bridge's fallback BLS attestation circuit, plus a sample
proof + public-input vector that the producer round-trip test
verified end-to-end (`verify_proof::<KZG, VerifierSHPLONK, …,
Blake2bRead, SingleStrategy>` returns `Ok(true)`) before exporting.

| File | Size | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `fallback_vk_blob.bin` | 6 308 B | Ready-to-load `vk_cell` payload — drop into a TVM cell verbatim. |
| `fallback_public_inputs.bin` | 128 B | 4 × 32 B LE Fr (bk_set_commit, env_hash_hi, env_hash_lo, last_seen_seqno). |
| `fallback_proof.bin` | 14 784 B | SHPLONK proof + Blake2b transcript, K=20. |
| `fallback_vk.bin` | 6 154 B | Raw `VerifyingKey` for partners who want to assemble their own `VkBlob`. |
| `fallback_config_params.json` | 181 B | Matching `BaseCircuitParams`. |

The same three fixture files are checked in on the consumer side at
`tvm-sdk/tvm_vm/halo2_test_data/fallback_*.bin` and exercised by
`test_halo2_with_vk::bridge_circuit_1b_fallback_real_proof_verifies`
(passes; CI green on PR #243).

## Smoke test (Rust producer side)

```bash
cd acki-nacki-bridge
cargo test -p bridge-snark-utils --lib   # 6 unit tests, ~1 s
cargo test -p bridge-snark-utils --test halo2_tvm_bundle_round_trip --release  # ~5 min with cached keys
```

## Smoke test (Rust consumer side, tvm-sdk PR #243)

```bash
cd tvm-sdk
cargo test -p tvm_vm --lib --tests test_halo2_with_vk  # 12 tests, ~6 s
cargo test -p tvm_vm --lib zk_halo2_with_vk_bundle     # 9 VkBlob unit tests
```

## Open items still pending your ack

- **Q-GAS-1** — current gas price `5_000` is a structural placeholder
  modelled on `VERGRTH16_GAS_PRICE = 2_380`. Needs re-benchmarking
  against the cached / cold-cache verify wall-clock at K=20 before
  mainnet. Fixture in `fixtures/` is large enough to benchmark realistically.
- **Q-TRANS-1** — would you prefer Keccak transcript as an alternate
  flavour (reserved as `transcript_kind = 0x01`)? Default stays
  Blake2b; switching is a one-byte change in the `VkBlob` header.

